  "title": "fc-poisson-2",
  "abstract": "A machine-checked proof that the Poisson conjecture fails for two canonical pairs, and hence for every n >= 2, following the explicit counterexample of C. D. Long (2026). The statements and definitions are Formal Conjectures' (PoissonConjecture.lean, arXiv math/0608009), copied verbatim into Challenge.lean, so this entry proves Formal Conjectures' own statements.",
